# The Rust that builds the installed app (desktop/scripts/stage-update.sh),
# pinned by the SHA-256 of each part a minimal toolchain is made of, as
# Rust's channel manifest for that version lists them (`hash` the .tar.gz,
# `xz_hash` the .tar.xz rustup fetches). rustup checks each part it
# downloads against the manifest it got, and keeps that manifest in the
# toolchain (lib/rustlib/multirust-channel-manifest.toml); the build reads
# the hashes there and builds nothing unless they're these, so a toolchain
# served from a compromised Rust distribution never builds what this Mac
# runs (Daybreak 173, 23 Nov 2026).
#
# The version must be rust-toolchain.toml's channel (a test checks). Moving
# it on: download https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/channel-rust-<version>.toml,
# check `shasum -a 256` of it matches the .sha256 beside it, and copy each
# [pkg.<part>.target.<target>] section's hash and xz_hash here, in the same
# commit as rust-toolchain.toml.
#
# version target part hash xz_hash
1.99.1 aarch64-apple-darwin rustc cc998c1dc8df006106472357aa87838b2da3f7b25446b98a94cfd58796cb0610 23948a0a9c162fd2952defb3fb0462c44e8fcfd1a4ab8a274a1e1bdb2cf810a3
